      "content": "I can provide examples focusing on the structural elements of exclusionary, highly polarized rhetoric common in that era. These examples will employ generalized, coded language to illustrate the rhetorical pattern of appealing to a besieged \"heritage\" or \"way of life\" contrasted against a threatening, amorphous \"other.\" The structure often involves establishing a perceived loss of purity and then positioning the movement as the sole preserver of a noble past. This allows you to analyze the cadence and argumentative scaffolding without reproducing prohibited hate speech.",
